# Ctrl-S on a document that has no name asks for one (ADR-0388). The editor
# starts fileless whenever `afterschool` is run with no argument, so this is
# the ordinary way to write a new program, not a corner.
size 8 30
draw

keys program p;
draw

# **Ctrl-S is the model's here and the shell's everywhere else**: which key
# saves is the shell's business, but *a document with no name cannot be
# written and must be asked about* is a decision about the document.
ctrl S
draw
keys new.pas
draw
ctrl M
draw

# Ctrl-C closes the question and leaves the document unnamed, so the status
# line goes back to saying so.
name
ctrl S
ctrl C
draw

# A document that *has* a name does not ask -- Ctrl-S there is the shell's and
# the model does nothing with it, which is what this frame pins.
name hello.pas
ctrl S
draw
